## Execution

1. Review this plan (`commit.md`) and the generated script (`commit.sh`).
2. Preview the actions without making any changes (dry-run is default):
   ```bash
   ./commit.sh
   ```
3. When ready, execute the script with `--run` to apply commits, create branches, and submit PRs:
   ```bash
   ./commit.sh --run
   ```
4. Verify the created stack:
   ```bash
   gh stack view --json
   ```
